WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.536
JEREMY: 251 to go.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.872
CHRIS: 251 meters.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.143
NARRATOR: Team Russia,
three tough as nails
cops from Anchorage,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.277
are tied for second place.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.380
CHRIS: We're ready to go.
We're excited about today.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.482
We got our two
points on day two,

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.351
so we plan on getting
two points day three.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.387
CHRIS: Or, Jeremy
said we don't get to eat.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.288
JEREMY: In between
the two rocks?

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.656
CHRIS: Yeah, but I
think we go around.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:27.127
NARRATOR: Starting just
outside the industrial
town of Irkutsk,

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.329
the fiercely
competitive trio biked,

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:35.301
rode and drove 250
kilometers across frigid
tundra onto Olkhon Island,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.437
a grassy oasis in the
largest freshwater

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.671
lake in the world.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.674
With only three points so far,
they're itching to prove

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.309
they're the team to beat.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.577
JEREMY: Like,
without being a dick,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.212
are we able to push
the pace at all?

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.213
Or no?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.615
ANGELINA: It sounds like
a dickish thing to say.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.883
CHRIS: What did she say?

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.317
JEREMY: She said
I'm being a dick.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:54.621
CHRIS: Somehow the three
of us found each other,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.490
and at our nature,
at our center point,

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:01.394
we were born with sarcasm,
competition,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.597
and just a little
bit not nice.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.101
JEREMY: We've reached it.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.538
ANGELINA: Look to your right.
It is so amazing.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.473
CHRIS: Oh, look at that.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.342
NARRATOR: Today, their course
will take them off the island

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.278
aboard a transport boat.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.581
But, first, they've got
to get down to the beach.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.150
ANGELINA: We are
getting ready to rappel down

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.386
this beautiful cliff here.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.156
NARRATOR: To get to the water,
the team will first each solo

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:34.694
rappel 80 meters of loose dirt
and granite to an anchor tree.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:38.898
Then, descend 60 meters
of uneven terrain to
another solo rappel,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:42.502
which will drop
them onto the beach.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.237
ANGELINA: I know it's
fun to go fast,

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.439
but I don't want to kick
rocks down on folks.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.344
CHRIS: Alright,
I see the tree.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.712
Here we go.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:53.713
NARRATOR: First
to take the leap,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.150
42-year-old canine
officer Chris Nelson.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.524
CHRIS: The rope is caught,
got it undone.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:08.528
We had a reserve unit
at the marine corps
in Anchorage, Alaska.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:12.632
They put us through rappelling,
rock climbing, parachuting.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:16.703
I was taught how to do it
safely and in a smart way.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.444
CHRIS: Rock!

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:26.813
NARRATOR: With Chris
safely through,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:31.150
next up is 13 year veteran
officer, Jeremy Conkling.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.152
JEREMY: Awesome, ready to go.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:37.190
My rappelling experience prior
to today has been all while

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.391
I was on SWAT.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.160
Ever since I was a little
kid playing cops and robbers,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.428
never wanted to be the robber.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.430
Always wanted to be
the police officer.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.698
Always wanted to be on SWAT.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.500
That was always
my goal, my dream.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.169
The danger of the job
certainly is something that

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.437
attracted me to it.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.173
Just being the person that is
reliable in intense situations

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.310
and the person that is there
to help others when they're

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.145
having the worst
day of their life.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.347
CHRIS:
I like your technique.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:04.150
Beautiful rappel.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:11.791
ANGELINA: The only rappelling
I did is like a rope course,

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.661
like a challenge course,
in high school.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.795
NARRATOR: The final
team member to hook in,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:19.299
42-year-old Angie Frazie,
a rookie on the ropes,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.801
but no stranger to
blazing a trail.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.002
ANGELINA: Let's do it.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.371
It's not always easy, and
sometimes it's lonely being a

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.807
police officer that's a girl,
cause gender is always there.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.343
Any woman will tell you
that's the case.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.312
You know, I just have a
competitive personality,

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.580
so it doesn't matter
if they're boys,

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.214
or girls, or whatever.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.417
I'm going to try to be
the best at something.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.119
Woo, rock.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.589
CHRIS: That's on me.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.691
Oh god, they're
in the shoulder.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:49.295
JEREMY: Can I get a
helmet for my shoulder?

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.564
CHRIS: Made it.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.833
You yelled rock,
and we got in place

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.536
just in time to take
it in the shoulder.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:04:00.740
So, knowing that we still
have 11 days in front of us,

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:04.444
the majority of this
race is still to come.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.778
JEREMY: A million dollars
would be amazing.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.313
It could pay off
my law school,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.082
I've got a few years
left in law school.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:12.151
And, to know that that's all
paid for would be fantastic.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.559
CHRIS: Did you guys
look that good?

